From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: handle i2c client creation errors

i2c_new_client_device() returns an ERR_PTR on failure. The recovered
vendor flow treats the result as a plain pointer and dereferences it, so
starting tx-isp before the DT sensor driver has bound (the address is
already claimed) panics the kernel on -EBUSY.

Handle the error pointer the same way the vendor i2c_new_device() NULL
return is handled.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t31/tx_isp_module.c
+++ b/driver/t31/tx_isp_module.c
@@ -944,7 +944,7 @@
 #else
     client = i2c_new_client_device(adapter, info);
 #endif
-    if (!client)
+    if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(client))
         return NULL;
 
     /* Stock: dev = *(client + 0x1c) - get client->dev */
